{
  "importance": "magnitude_l2",
  "export_path": "onnx2tf",
  "importance_and_path_evidence": "Neither was recorded on the rows, which carry `model` and `channel_ratio_pct` rather than a stem. Both are read off results/tflite_size_audit.json: the 18 channel-era line_seg artifacts (the stems WITHOUT the `_param` suffix that the round-2 parameter ladder added) all end in `_magnitude_l2` and all carry `export_path: onnx2tf`. The three rows here that carry `compiled` are the 90% rung of each backbone, which is line_seg_{base128,link_r34,w96}_pruned90pct_magnitude_l2 in that audit.",
 "note": "Channel-ratio sweep for the three line-seg models. The 27 rows with finetuned=true are the full 10-90% grid from one HPC cluster batch job (2026-08-14, 48m23s, 27/27 OK), recovery FT = the upstream `mix` recipe verbatim (AdamW lr 8e-4, 30 ep, 3000 samples/ep, pos_weight 12). The 8 rows with finetuned=false are an earlier, un-finetuned dense sampling around the on-chip residency boundary (w96 22-28%, link_r34 52-58%); they carry byte/structure numbers only, which is why val_iou is null there.",
 "superseded_by": "results/line_seg/param_ladder_oncar.json -- the round-2 ladder, on PARAMETER ratio semantics, compiled and timed on a Coral. This file is the retired round-1 CHANNEL-ratio ladder that the ratio-semantics section of docs/PRUNING_HAZARDS.md refers to as what `--ratio_semantics channel` reproduces; the section does not link it, and nothing in the repo reads it.",
 "ratio_semantics": "channel_ratio_pct is a PER-LAYER CHANNEL ratio, not a parameter ratio; params fall as (1-r)^2. Compare families via param_reduction_pct.",
 "metrics": "val_iou / floor_fire are FLOAT held-out numbers under the upstream protocol (n_track=38, n_floor=58). floor_fire is a count out of 58, so 0.0172 == exactly one frame.",
 "compiled_note": "`compiled` present only where an Edge TPU build exists (the three 90% rows).",
